# Microsoft Copilot Studio and Power Platform: The 2025–2026 Landscape

Microsoft's Power Platform underwent a structural transformation in 2025–2026. Copilot Studio evolved from a chatbot builder into a full AI agent orchestration platform. Generative orchestration became the default paradigm, agent flows introduced Copilot Credit–based billing, multi-agent collaboration matured, and Teams integration deepened.

Simultaneously:

- **Power Apps** adopted an agent-first architecture with generative pages and MCP server support.
- **Power Automate** remained the deterministic execution backbone connecting agents to enterprise systems.

This document covers major capabilities, limits, architectural patterns, and integration models as of February 2026.

---

# Generative Orchestration: LLM-Driven Planning Replaces Trigger Phrases

Generative orchestration became GA for English agents in March 2025 and is now the default for new agents.

## Core Architectural Shift

Classic trigger-phrase matching is replaced with:

- An LLM-driven planning layer
- Intent interpretation
- Automatic topic/tool selection
- Multi-step execution with guardrails

Instead of defining “User says X,” makers now define **topic descriptions**. The orchestrator uses:

- Topic name
- Topic description
- Input/output parameter names and descriptions
- Conversation context

…to determine routing.

When migrating classic agents, descriptions are auto-generated from trigger phrases, though manual refinement is recommended.

## Capabilities

- Multi-intent handling in a single turn
- Sequential chaining of topics and tools
- Custom agent instructions influencing planning
- Activity map for inspecting execution during testing
- Model selection:
  - GPT-4.1 (default as of Oct 2025)
  - GPT-5 Chat GA (Nov 2025, EU/US)
  - GPT-5 Reasoning (preview)
  - Experimental models

## Key Limitations

- No Conversational Boosting system topic
- No custom entities (closed lists, regex) as tool inputs
- No “Multiple Topics Matched” disambiguation topic
- Limited conversation history window
- Maximum 128 tools per agent (25–30 recommended)

